lently testing a stale `.so`. Added `assert_fresh()` which refuses to run if `libdriver.so` is older than `src/lib.rs`, plus `run_all.sh` always builds first.\n\nAlso replaced `ptr.add(usize::MAX)` (UB) with `wrapping_add`, which computes the same address the C's `outDirName[strlen(outDirName)-1]` reads on an empty `outDirName` — that out-of-bounds read is reproduced deliberately, tested with the preceding byte pinned to both `'/'` and non-`'/'`.\n\n### Anti-vacuity check\nRe-ran the suite against 6 deliberate mutations: all 4 real behaviour changes were caught (including \"fixing\" the empty-`outDirName` OOB read and the `'\\0'`-separator quirk); the 2 behaviourally-equivalent rewrites were correctly not flagged. Details in **`REPORT.md`**.\n\n`c_src/` sources were not modified (only the prescribed `c_src/build/` output exists)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":462,"cache_read_input_tokens":116016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":462,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"19c425ee-cc37-46c2-9e5d-e212fa01a7ac","uuid":"ce44bb77-4efa-4b8b-a7c7-537478d3b8c5","timestamp":"2026-08-20T13:17:02.693Z"}
